{
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "You wake beside a ruin of Heliodor with empty hands. A compass is waiting for you, and so is an Atlas."
  ],
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.title": "Waking among ruins",
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Use the pedestal at the heart of the ruin to take the Heliodor Compass, then pick a nearby site with water, wood and room to grow. Quests open with F8 or the book icon in your inventory; confirm once you have read this.",
    "Tuff cut by machines, copper veins gone dark, gardens that kept growing with nobody to tend them. Whoever lived here left all at once."
  ],
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.title": "Somewhere to begin",
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Craft a crafting table. Before spending materials, check a recipe's uses in the recipe viewer.",
    "The ruin kept its stones, not its tools. Whatever Heliodor knew, you start again from wood."
  ],
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.title": "Read the stone",
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a stone pickaxe. Check the block overlay before mining an unfamiliar ore: tool tier matters.",
    "The ruin's tuff was cut with machines, not chisels. Some day you will need that kind of precision too."
  ],
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.title": "A recipe worth keeping",
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Bookmark a recipe you plan to make next in the recipe viewer (its keys are listed in Controls), remove finished ones so the list stays useful, and confirm.",
    "A short list of what comes next: that is how Heliodor's workshops started every morning."
  ],
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.title": "A shelf for tomorrow",
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a chest. Keep your next project's materials apart, and try the sorting and matching-deposit controls on ordinary items.",
    "Among the loose pages, a copper seal with a golden A: 'Council inventory. Everything is recorded.' Somebody here counted everything."
  ],
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.title": "Heat with a purpose",
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Build a furnace and smelt or cook a useful batch; prepare the inputs before lighting it.",
    "Supply, transform, collect: Heliodor ran whole cities on that pattern, fed by the sun instead of coal."
  ],
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.title": "The edge of the dark",
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Prepare eight torches and light the path between your entrance, water and workshop before you go underground.",
    "A loose page carries a blessing, signed with a single letter: 'May the light find you at home. —B.'"
  ],
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.title": "A return address",
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Place and use a bed once you can get wool safely; keep the respawn space clear and tell your companions where it is. Confirm when done.",
    "In the ruin, nobody switched the lights off. Whoever lived there meant to come back that same night."
  ],
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.title": "The Atlas listens",
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Click the task to open the Atlas, pick The Atlas Awakens and deliver a book and a copper ingot. You get a Living Atlas to come back to it.",
    "The cover warms up. A voice pushes through the static: '…make room for… &kthose&r who… have not arrived.'"
  ],
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.title": "Carry the river",
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Smelt iron for a bucket and bring water to a small farm beside your shelter.",
    "Heliodor's gardens still drink from channels nobody tends. Water was the first thing its people learned to move."
  ],
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.title": "The patient part",
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Harvest three wheat and replant before you leave; keep seeds apart from food.",
    "A note in careful green ink: 'Sow extra. Someone hungry always turns up. —J.'"
  ],
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.title": "A kitchen tool",
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Make a flint knife and check its uses: Farmer's Delight knives work on the cutting board and gather certain ingredients.",
    "The ruin's kitchens were built for crowds. Whoever ran them fed far more people than ever lived here."
  ],
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.title": "A different kind of crafting",
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Place a cutting board, put an ingredient on it and use the tool its recipe shows.",
    "In Heliodor even a kitchen board was a small machine: something goes in, one gesture, something useful comes out."
  ],
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.title": "Four places at the table",
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Prepare four bowls. Some meals give the bowl back, so count them when you plan a batch.",
    "The ruin's tables are laid for more guests than chairs. J. wrote underneath: 'A kitchen is measured by who it can welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.title": "Food before distance",
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Bake three bread for a short survey and watch saturation as well as hunger. Keep a reserve at home.",
    "J.'s packing lists always start with bread, 'for whoever gets lost'."
  ],
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.title": "A table for those returning",
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select A Table for Travellers, check what is missing and choose Deliver.",
    "J. always kept a place set for strangers. The Atlas answers the delivery with one clear word through the noise: '…welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.title": "Metal that remembers weather",
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four copper ingots and keep them with the glass for the lens.",
    "Every instrument in the ruin has a copper frame gone green. Someone designed them to be repaired, not replaced."
  ],
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.title": "A window small enough to carry",
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four glass, taking sand from a small, safe patch rather than undermining your shelter.",
    "Heliodor built with glass so the light could reach everything. It was what its people loved most."
  ],
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.title": "A borrowed horizon",
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select Assemble the Lens and deliver the listed materials to receive the raw lens once. Keep it for the first signal.",
    "Beside the sketch, in a small, precise hand: 'Measure before believing. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.title": "Mark the ordinary",
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Find the map's controls, mark your shelter with a practical name and confirm.",
    "The Atlas remembers a world that no longer matches yours. Your own map is the one that tells the truth today."
  ],
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.title": "Leave with a question",
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Prepare three paper for field notes, and pack food, a pickaxe and light with room left for samples.",
    "The compass will not send you far. Heliodor's traces are close, if you know how to look."
  ],
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.title": "Two accounts of one place",
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Take a short walk and compare a nearby landmark with your map, then open Field Survey in the Atlas and deliver its materials (paper and an ordinary compass) to receive your survey notes.",
    "What the villagers remember and what the Atlas remembers do not match. Somebody has to write it down again."
  ],
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.title": "The expedition ends at home",
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Back home, restock food and torches before storing the rest, try matching-deposit and note one material you were missing. Confirm when done.",
    "Every trip in J.'s notes ends the same way: 'Back home. Nobody lost.'"
  ],
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.title": "One light answers",
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Open First Signal in the Atlas and deliver the listed materials. Your team receives a signal core once: use it to build a survey station.",
    "Far away, a light answers. Through the static, a voice: '…can you &khear&r… us? We are still… here.'"
  ],
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.title": "A workshop with a destination",
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "When every project of this act is delivered, choose Advance in the Atlas to open the next one; if it takes too long, choose Refresh before retrying. Confirm to close the act.",
    "The voice has gone quiet. Once you advance, the compass will turn toward a workshop that sank with its tools inside."
  ],
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.title": "A place your compass remembers",
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Build a survey station from the signal core, copper, smooth stone and glass. Use an ordinary compass on it to mark the spot without spending the compass (it points here within this dimension); an empty hand opens your team's Atlas.",
    "Heliodor had a station like this in every square. The Heliodor Compass follows the Atlas; this one brings you home."
  ],
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A workshop the earth swallowed keeps Heliodor's crafts: measuring, powering, growing and feeding. Someone once brought them to one bench."
  ],
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.title": "Four benches, one workshop",
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Pick any branch below. Hexagonal tasks open the Atlas, and only a delivery there moves your team's story; the rest are lessons. Confirm when ready.",
    "The signal led to a workshop the earth swallowed. Four benches, four crafts, and one name scratched into every one: Terra."
  ],
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.title": "Let water do the turning",
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Craft a Create water wheel from planks around a shaft, and use its Ponder scene to set it in flowing water.",
    "Terra's first note starts with a stream, not a furnace: 'Borrow a force before you make one.'"
  ],
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.title": "An iron ingot, made flat",
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Connect a mechanical press to rotation with a depot under its head, as Ponder shows, and press iron ingots into two iron sheets for a calibration frame.",
    "In the Sunken Workshop the presses still stand in a row, rusted mid-stroke."
  ],
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.title": "Read the strain",
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Make Engineer's Goggles (glass, string and a gold plate from your press), wear them and compare a machine's speed and stress before adding another.",
    "Terra crossed out 'make it turn faster' and wrote 'measure first'. Somebody above her kept asking for more."
  ],
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.title": "Wire without a factory",
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "With Immersive Engineering's hammer turn a copper ingot into a plate, then use its wirecutters to make copper wire. You need two for the frame.",
    "A hand route for when the machines are gone. Terra always left one."
  ],
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.title": "A Measure of Iron",
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Craft a calibration frame (two iron sheets, two copper wires and a raw lens) and deliver it to Precision Bench in the Atlas. You will need a second frame later.",
    "Terra's standard joins hand tools and machines in one measure. The same frame holds Heliodor's lens in its solar heating plates."
  ],
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.title": "A small electrical beginning",
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Actually Additions coal generator (iron casings with black quartz, iron and wooden rods) and keep fuel nearby.",
    "A soot-stained page: 'Coal, for now. Until the sun. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.title": "A beam with a job",
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Atomic Reconstructor (iron casing, iron and redstone), power it and test it with one redstone dust where drops are easy to recover.",
    "Heliodor shaped matter with light long before it tried to shape anything bigger."
  ],
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.title": "Redstone remembers another shape",
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Beam redstone dust into ordinary Restonia crystals (40 energy each). Keep two, with an iron casing and two Create andesite alloys, for an energy coupler.",
    "The crystals hum at the same pitch as the Atlas. Terra noticed too; her margin only says: 'Why?'"
  ],
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.title": "A Crystal Connection",
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Craft an energy coupler from two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys, and deliver it to Crystal Grid in the Atlas. Your generator and reconstructor stay installed.",
    "With the coupler, Heliodor turned rotation into current. Every generator coil it built asks for one."
  ],
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.title": "Write a first working spell",
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make a novice spell book from a book and a spare iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword, then try a utility spell somewhere safe.",
    "Beside Terra's machines, someone kept a quieter shelf of prayers and spells, signed with a single letter: B."
  ],
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.title": "Keep a source-gem reserve",
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make Ars source gems by imbuing amethyst or lapis in an imbuement chamber (archwood planks and gold). The living matrix needs two.",
    "B. wrote that magic is tended, not squeezed. The workshop's gem beds were never emptied."
  ],
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.title": "A crop with workshop uses",
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "At an Enchanting Apparatus (diamond, gold and sourcestone), a seed with four source gems makes magebloom seeds; the listed Source cost is zero. Grow a bed and craft the blooms into fibers: keep two.",
    "A flower grown to be woven into machines. Heliodor never quite saw a line between the two."
  ],
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.title": "The living workshop",
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Craft a living matrix (two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a new calibration frame) and deliver it to Living Workshop in the Atlas after Precision Bench.",
    "Terra's measurements drawn over B.'s garden bed: the only page in the workshop signed by both."
  ],
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.title": "The kitchen keeps working",
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Build a Farmer's Delight cooking pot (iron, bricks, a water bucket and a wooden shovel), set it over heat and cook a batch from nearby crops.",
    "J.'s list puts a cooking pot before any second machine. A workshop runs on whoever feeds it."
  ],
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.title": "Use the catch",
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Fillet a catch with an Aquaculture knife and cook the fillets on a campfire, in a furnace or in a smoker. Save some for rations.",
    "The workshop's canal still has fish. J. stocked it himself, the note says, 'for the long shifts'."
  ],
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.title": "Pack a real travelling meal",
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets make one pack of Travel Rations; the soup takes carrot, potato, beetroot and leafy-green tags.",
    "J. packed these for workers who were not allowed to go home. The note does not say who gave that order."
  ],
  "quest.774DD93299251487.title": "The travelling pantry",
  "quest.774DD93299251487.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one pack of Travel Rations to Travelling Pantry. No pot, rod or other equipment is taken.",
    "J.'s note ends with a correction: 'Count the people who come back, not the crates that leave.'"
  ],
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.title": "Can the next person repeat it?",
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Optional: press a second iron ingot, label the press's input and output, and leave a note on what to check if rotation stops. Confirm after trying it.",
    "Terra wrote every procedure 'for the next one'. She never expected to be the one missing."
  ],
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.title": "Leave the bed ready",
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest a small magebloom batch, process some fibers and leave the bed planted, with seeds and spare fibers stored apart. Confirm after trying it.",
    "B.'s rule for any garden: leave it ready for someone else's hands."
  ],
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.title": "The room in the records",
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "With the four projects delivered, bring three paper and one copper ingot to the Atlas and deliver Workshop Archive. The Atlas hands you Terra's Arm, which lengthens your reach while worn.",
    "The Sunken Workshop agrees at last: no craft ever replaced the others. And through the static, for the first time, the voice says its own name: '…&kTe&rrra.'"
  ],
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.title": "A workshop worth connecting",
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Optional: choose one supply worth improving (sheets, crystals, fibers or provisions) and keep the other benches working. When the act is complete, choose Advance in the Atlas.",
    "Terra's workshop fed routes she never drew. The next pages follow where everything went."
  ],
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Under a broken glass dome a garden still blooms. Heliodor's routes started here and led to a capital no map shows."
  ],
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.title": "The silence between workshops",
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "Five projects below rebuild Heliodor's routes: hexagons open the Atlas, squares teach the materials and circles are optional trials. Confirm when ready.",
    "Under the Greenhouse Dome, Juan's trees still flower. His ledgers show food leaving here for every city, and above all for one: Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.title": "Presses from the fallen sky",
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Break a meteorite's mysterious cube without Silk Touch to get the four AE2 presses (a charged meteorite compass points to one), then print and assemble two logic processors in a powered Inscriber.",
    "Heliodor's routes spoke a language of circuits. The presses fell from the sky; Terra only learned to read them."
  ],
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.title": "A board takes several benches",
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Assemble a PneumaticCraft PCB from an unassembled board, two capacitors and two transistors, following its guide for plastic, UV exposure, etching acid and pressures. The Amadron PCB blueprint costs eight emeralds.",
    "Every route in Juan's ledgers has a board like this at each end, so either side could repair it."
  ],
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.title": "A blue signal",
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Beam lapis into ordinary Palis crystals at the Atomic Reconstructor (40 energy each). Two go into a routing matrix, with two logic processors, a PCB and a calibration frame.",
    "Blue was the colour of Heliodor's routes. On the old maps, every blue line ends at the same blank spot."
  ],
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.title": "Budget the first crystal",
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Four inferium around an infusion crystal make one prudentium; the crystal costs a diamond, four prosperity shards and four inferium. Budget eight additional inferium for two prudentium.",
    "Juan grew essences the way he grew wheat: planted, counted, never all at once."
  ],
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.title": "Wax from an ordinary hive",
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Process ordinary Minecraft honeycomb into wax in a basic Productive Bees centrifuge (iron and a grindstone). Two wax, no special breeding.",
    "The Greenhouse Dome still hums. Juan's bees outlived everyone who kept them."
  ],
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.title": "The old garden contributes",
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Make another living matrix (a calibration frame, two source gems and two magebloom fibers): the act II one was consumed. With two prudentium and two wax it becomes a propagation core.",
    "Juan's notes grow into B.'s garden bed: the two of them planned this greenhouse together."
  ],
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.title": "Osmium learns a signal",
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Infuse an osmium ingot with 20 redstone infusion in a powered Metallurgic Infuser to make a basic control circuit. A power regulator needs two.",
    "A small generator is enough. Heliodor spread its power thin on purpose, so no single failure could take everything."
  ],
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.title": "Steel without a giant furnace",
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Hammer a steel ingot into an Immersive Engineering steel plate; Mekanism's carbon infusion (enriched iron, steel dust, then smelting) is an early route to the ingot. Keep two plates.",
    "The dome's frame is steel under copper. It held the glass up for years after the people were gone."
  ],
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.title": "A coupling, not a power plant",
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Rebuild an energy coupler (two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys). With two circuits and two steel plates it makes a power regulator.",
    "The same coupling Terra drew in the Sunken Workshop, now feeding a whole greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.title": "Read the tree before the shelf",
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Squeeze a Menril log for 1000 mB of resin, dry it in a Drying Basin into a crystallized Menril block, and craft the block into nine chunks. Keep two.",
    "Juan planted Menril along every route, so the roads themselves could keep count."
  ],
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.title": "Bake the logic",
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Craft four raw LaserIO logic chips from a quartz block, clay balls, gold nuggets and redstone, and smelt them into finished chips. The sensor needs two.",
    "Clay and gold, baked like bread. Some of Heliodor's best ideas came out of its kitchens."
  ],
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.title": "A second matrix has a job",
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Make another routing matrix (two logic processors, a PCB, two Palis crystals and a calibration frame): the first went to A Shared Language. With two Menril chunks and two finished chips it makes an inventory sensor.",
    "A route that knows when it is full needs nobody shouting at it. Juan's ledgers say that took years to learn."
  ],
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.title": "Paper tells the hands",
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Craft six blank Modular Routers modules from paper, gold nuggets and redstone; keep two for the handling core and configure the rest for real jobs.",
    "In Heliodor, instructions were written on paper first, and only then given to a machine."
  ],
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.title": "Five careful passes",
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Start a Create precision mechanism with a gold plate, then deploy a small cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget in order, five times (deployers need brass hands; see Ponder). The result is probabilistic: keep spare inputs.",
    "Terra's hand shows in every Heliodor mechanism: patient, repeatable, never quite trusting luck."
  ],
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.title": "A regulator for the hands",
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Make a second power regulator (two basic circuits, two steel plates and an energy coupler); the first was delivered. With two blank modules and a precision mechanism it makes a handling core.",
    "Hands that pass a part along and keep their tools: Juan's crews worked that way, from dome to dome."
  ],
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.title": "Label the destination",
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Optional: pick one workshop input, label its source, destination and spare stock, and send a small batch its receiver can recognise unaided. Confirm after trying it.",
    "Every crate in Juan's ledgers carries a destination. The ones bound for Solsticio carry a golden seal as well."
  ],
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.title": "Leave another harvest possible",
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest one crop batch and one ordinary hive batch, and keep back what each needs to produce again. Confirm after trying it.",
    "Juan never shipped his last seed. 'The city can wait a week,' he wrote. 'The field cannot wait a year.'"
  ],
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.title": "Watch a whole batch",
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Optional: run a small infuser batch and compare its energy buffer before and after; keep spare fuel or a second source. Confirm after watching it.",
    "Heliodor's glass roofs once caught the sun for machines like these. None of them ever ran on a single source."
  ],
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.title": "Stop before overflow",
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Optional: with Integrated Dynamics and Integrated Tunnels, or LaserIO, read a buffer and stop insertion at a small threshold, then watch it resume. Confirm after observing it.",
    "Every pipe in the greenhouse has a valve Juan could close by hand. He never trusted a store that could not say 'enough'."
  ],
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.title": "Thirty-two arrive together",
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Optional: move 32 ordinary items between containers with configured Modular Routers modules or a Create setup, and account for all of them at the other end. Confirm once all 32 arrive.",
    "Juan counted crews the way he counted crates: everyone who left had to arrive."
  ],
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.title": "A Shared Language",
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Deliver one routing matrix to A Shared Language in the Atlas. It also gives you an Altar of Peace, which keeps hostile creatures from spawning around it.",
    "Different benches agree on a destination again. The Atlas voice, clearer now: 'Terra here. If you &kcan&r read this… the routes… still work.'"
  ],
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.title": "Seeds of Continuity",
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Deliver one propagation core to Seeds of Continuity in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Growth: crops around it grow much faster and yield more.",
    "Juan designed that altar to feed a Heliodor that never stopped growing. His greenhouse fed multitudes; now it can feed you."
  ],
  "quest.55E5576006404510.title": "Power without a Monolith",
  "quest.55E5576006404510.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Deliver one power regulator to Power without a Monolith in the Atlas. Regulators are also what Create's advanced solar heating plates, energisers and motors ask for.",
    "Terra's drawing leaves room for many small suns instead of one great one. Someone wrote 'inefficient' across it, in gold ink."
  ],
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.title": "When the Shelf is Full",
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Deliver one inventory sensor to When the Shelf is Full in the Atlas.",
    "A full shelf can warn before it jams. Juan's routes did; the orders from Solsticio never waited for the answer."
  ],
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.title": "Small Hands, Large Workshops",
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Deliver one handling core to Small Hands, Large Workshops in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Levelling, which flattens the ground around it, moving earth without creating any.",
    "Heliodor levelled its terraces with this altar and planted every one. The fields went on; the people did not."
  ],
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.title": "Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "After the five projects, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to Exchange Route in the Atlas to close the act.",
    "Every route ends at Solsticio, the capital, and Solsticio is on no map. Terra's voice: 'Look up. The city &mfell&r… did not fall. It is &kstill&r… here.'"
  ],
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From an observatory on a cliff, Heliodor watched the sky. In the Temple of the Sacred Light it tried to seize it. In the Aether, the Sun Spirit stopped it."
  ],
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.title": "The missing witnesses",
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "Four routes below lead to this act's Atlas projects, and a fifth ends at the Sun Spirit; arrivals in other worlds are recorded on their own when your team gets there. Confirm when ready.",
    "The Cliffside Observatory still points at the same patch of sky. Its log ends on a single line: 'The light answered.'"
  ],
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.title": "Aether: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Aether with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. Clicking this task does nothing: the server records the journey.",
    "The Observatory's telescope pointed here. Heliodor went up to ask the sky a question."
  ],
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.title": "Twilight Forest: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Twilight Forest with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to deliver.",
    "Heliodor's gardeners called this forest the rehearsal: a world where the light never quite arrives. Juan kept a sanctuary here."
  ],
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.title": "Bumblezone: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Bumblezone with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to claim.",
    "Juan's bees came from here. Heliodor signed a treaty with them, and the bees still keep their side."
  ],
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.title": "A crystal tuned to listening",
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Spirit Fire (drop datura and light it with flint and steel), turn four diamonds into four spirit-attuned gems in it, and craft the gems 2×2 into one spirit-attuned crystal.",
    "The Observatory listened as well as looked. Its crystals still catch voices nobody is speaking."
  ],
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.title": "Two fragments of testimony",
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Malum's crude scythe (three iron ingots, one refined soulstone and two wooden rods) and kill a witch with it for arcane spirits. Keep two for each spectral lens.",
    "Every spirit the scythe frees carries a scrap of something it saw. Heliodor's scraps all end in the same flash."
  ],
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.title": "A patient shutter",
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Prepare one Create precision mechanism for the spectral lens; its assembly can fail, so budget a few attempts.",
    "The Observatory's shutter opened for one second a night. Terra built it; the order to open it wider came from someone else."
  ],
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.title": "The familiar frame",
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Craft a calibration frame from two iron sheets, two copper wires and a raw lens; the spectral lens consumes it.",
    "Terra's frame again, the same measure as in the first workshop. She built everything to fit together. That was the problem."
  ],
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.title": "Assemble the spectral lens",
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Combine a spirit-attuned crystal, two arcane spirits, a precision mechanism and a calibration frame into one spectral lens. Plan two lenses: the archive takes one and the containment seal another.",
    "Through the lens the static thins. You can hear several voices now, and one of them is giving orders."
  ],
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.title": "A route with a return",
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Optional: the Aether portal is a glowstone frame lit with water; the Twilight Forest opens when you throw a diamond into a 2×2 pool ringed with flowers (lightning strikes, so stand back). Pack food, mark the way home and confirm.",
    "The Observatory's charts mark both doors. Heliodor never went through one without a way back."
  ],
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.title": "Light above the clouds",
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Mine ambrosium ore in the Aether for two ambrosium shards, and keep them apart from your expedition supplies.",
    "The Aether's light is not the sun's. Heliodor noticed first, and wanted it."
  ],
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.title": "A forest worked into metal",
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft raw ironwood from liveroot, raw iron and a gold nugget, and smelt it into two ironwood ingots.",
    "Juan's sanctuary in the forest kept samples of everything, labelled with the place and the date. The last label has no date."
  ],
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.title": "Food for the record and the road",
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Make a spare pack of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets); the horizon chart consumes one, along with survey notes, which can be crafted again. Bring separate food to eat.",
    "Juan packed rations for the Observatory's night crews. The last order asked for double, 'for the ceremony'."
  ],
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.title": "Two skies on one page",
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft a horizon chart from two ambrosium shards, two ironwood ingots, survey notes and Travel Rations. Before delivering it, check that your team has arrived in both the Aether and the Twilight Forest.",
    "On one page, two skies that disagree about the colour of morning. The Observatory kept both."
  ],
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.title": "Enter as a guest",
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Optional: throw an ender pearl at a beehive or bee nest to enter the Bumblezone. Mark where you left and learn the way back first; hitting bees or taking honey carelessly brings Wrath. Confirm when ready.",
    "Juan's treaty had one clause: take nothing you cannot give back."
  ],
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.title": "Carry a little of the meadow",
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Gather two pollen puffs from pollen piles in the Bumblezone, using a tool without Silk Touch.",
    "Pollen from the treaty meadow. Juan's bees still remember the smell of the greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.title": "Wax from the treaty hives",
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two Productive Bees wax: ordinary honeycomb goes through the centrifuge, with no special breeding needed.",
    "The treaty was sealed in wax: Juan's way of saying it could be melted and made again."
  ],
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.title": "Two living supports",
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two living matrices, each from two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a calibration frame.",
    "Terra's frame, Juan's fibers, B.'s gems: the three of them still hold together in one object."
  ],
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.title": "A small agreement",
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Combine two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices into one ecosystem capsule.",
    "A whole meadow's agreement, small enough to carry. Heliodor's Altar of Renewal was built around one of these."
  ],
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.title": "A dark edge for the vessel",
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Mine EvilCraft dark ore for two dark gems; check the tool tier and the Origins of Darkness guide first.",
    "The Temple of the Sacred Light is ringed with dark stone. Its builders knew the light needed a boundary."
  ],
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.title": "Steel with a remembered purpose",
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "At Malum's Spirit Altar, an iron ingot, four refined soulstone, three wicked, one earthen and one arcane spirit make one soul-stained steel ingot. For two, gather eight refined soulstone, six wicked, two earthen and two arcane spirits.",
    "B. was Bodhi, the temple's priest. He forged the sanctuary's seals from this steel, and he was the one who said no."
  ],
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.title": "A second listening glass",
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft a second spectral lens for the containment seal, with the same crystal, spirits, mechanism and frame.",
    "One lens for the archive, one for the seal. Bodhi's note: 'Whatever you listen to, you must also be able to close.'"
  ],
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.title": "Keep the silence legible",
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Optional: set the archive's materials apart from the seal's and check which lens each one consumes. Confirm once they are separated.",
    "In the temple, one line of testimony stays unreadable. Bodhi left it that way on purpose: some gaps should not be filled with a convenient answer."
  ],
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.title": "Close the vessel gently",
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft one containment seal from two dark gems, two soul-stained steel ingots and a spectral lens; reactor rods for thorium fission ask for one as well.",
    "The seal is Bodhi's answer to the temple's machine: not a cage for the light, a boundary around it."
  ],
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.title": "Voices in the Glass",
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one spectral lens to Voices in the Glass; keep the second lens for the seal. Reinforced energisers and motors also take a spectral lens.",
    "The Observatory's crystal plays back a council session. A woman's voice, calm and certain: 'We will not worship the light. We will &mown&r… hold it.' The others call her Aurelia."
  ],
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.title": "Above and Beyond the Canopy",
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Aether and the Twilight Forest, deliver one horizon chart to Above and Beyond the Canopy in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Repose, a small chest that slowly mends the gear inside.",
    "The Observatory's last chart marks a point above the Aether's clouds, circled in gold: where the light came from."
  ],
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.title": "The Pollinators Agreement",
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Bumblezone, deliver one ecosystem capsule to The Pollinators Agreement in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Renewal, which rebuilds the land the world first generated around it.",
    "Juan's treaty still holds: the bees kept working after the witnesses left. Some promises outlive the people who made them."
  ],
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.title": "A Vessel for Restless Memory",
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "After Voices in the Glass, deliver one containment seal to A Vessel for Restless Memory in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Time: hostile creatures around it move in slow motion and drop far more.",
    "In the Temple of the Sacred Light the memory opens. Aurelia's council fused the sacred light with Terra's machines to build a god that would obey. Bodhi warned them; the crater is what his warning looked like."
  ],
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.title": "The Sun Spirit",
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Defeat a Sun Spirit in one of the Aether's gold dungeons; the compass leads there after the silver dungeon. Only its own ice crystals, struck back at it, can wound it. The first one your team defeats drops the Heart of Heliodor, and the server records it.",
    "It did not destroy Heliodor: it stopped it, and kept the Heart so no one could try again. Bodhi, through the noise: 'It was never &mtheirs&r… never anyone's to take.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.title": "A Clear Voice",
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Deliver the Heart of Heliodor to A Clear Voice in the Atlas. Only your team's own Heart counts, the one your Sun Spirit dropped. The Atlas keeps it; you will need it again in Solsticio.",
    "The crystal settles into the Atlas like a key into a lock, and the noise falls away. Terra, whole for the first time: 'There you are. We have always been able to hear you.'"
  ],
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.title": "The Atlas keeps their voices",
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "With the five projects recorded, the Heart among them, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to The Voices of the Atlas, then choose Advance.",
    "The temple's last page, read aloud at last: the fusion did not destroy Heliodor, because the Sun Spirit stopped it first and froze everyone inside the light. Terra: 'Now you know what we did. Help us leave without doing it again.'"
  ],
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.title": "V · The Ark",
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "With the Heart of Heliodor in the Atlas, the voice arrives whole: they are alive, inside the light. Build the Ark that opens the way without repeating the fusion."
  ],
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.title": "A whole voice",
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "The three projects below prepare the Ark's plan; its six modules, their batches and the activation follow in V · The Activation. Only deliveries in the Atlas record them. Confirm when ready.",
    "With the Heart in the Atlas, Terra's voice arrives whole: 'We are alive, inside the light. We call it the Entrelumen. Build the Ark, and this time do not try to own what you open.'"
  ],
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.title": "Two alloys for the bypass",
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Make two Mekanism atomic alloys in the Metallurgic Infuser: infused alloy with 20 diamond infusion gives reinforced alloy, and reinforced alloy with 40 refined-obsidian infusion gives atomic alloy.",
    "Terra designed the Ark's bus with a second path around every part. The fusion machine had none."
  ],
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.title": "A second path for the order",
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Prepare two PneumaticCraft printed circuit boards: an Empty PCB from the Pressure Chamber, exposed in a UV Light Box and etched, then assembled with two capacitors and two transistors.",
    "The boards that ran Juan's routes now carry the Ark's orders. Nothing in it is new, and that is the point."
  ],
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.title": "Keep the hands at work",
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Set aside two handling cores for the bus, each from two blank router modules, a precision mechanism and a power regulator.",
    "Hands that pass a part on and keep their tools. Terra wants the Ark built by many hands, never by one machine."
  ],
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.title": "Know what the buffer holds",
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Add one inventory sensor to the bus recipe: Menril chunks, LaserIO logic chips and a routing matrix, as in act III.",
    "The fusion drew power until nothing was left. The Ark has to know when it is full, and stop."
  ],
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.title": "A bus with a way around",
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "In a crafting grid combine two atomic alloys, two printed circuit boards, two handling cores and one inventory sensor: seven slots make one Ark Connection Bus. Modern Industrialization's nuclear reactor and Ad Astra's NASA workbench ask for one too.",
    "The Ark's spine. Terra: 'If one route fails, the others carry it. That is all I wanted from the start.'"
  ],
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.title": "Field note: empty, refill, resume",
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: label one input buffer, note its count, cut its supply and let a small job draw it down; restore it and check that the next batch finishes once. Confirm after observing it.",
    "A pause that can be resumed is what Heliodor lacked. The fusion had only one speed."
  ],
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.title": "A Network that Recovers",
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Deliver one Ark Connection Bus to A Network That Recovers in the Atlas.",
    "The first piece of the Ark is a way around failure. Terra, quietly: 'Aurelia asked me for a god. For you, I am building a door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.title": "Metal from an open sky",
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Make two Nature's Aura sky ingots at a flower-decorated Offering Table, using a Spirit of Calling crafted from Overworld and Nether aura bottles, a diamond, infused iron and tainted gold. Infused iron gives one ingot; tainted gold gives two.",
    "Juan grew metal under the open sky long before the council wanted the sky itself."
  ],
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.title": "A harvest with a ceiling",
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Prepare two imperium essences: four tertium around an infusion crystal make one, and each lower tier also takes four, so two imperium cost eight tertium, or 128 inferium.",
    "Juan's fear, even now inside the light, is running out. A reserve that grows back is his part of the Ark."
  ],
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.title": "Carry the habitat forward",
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Set aside two ecosystem capsules, each from two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices, as in act IV.",
    "The treaty meadow, carried into the Ark. Juan wants the bees to come along."
  ],
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.title": "Leave the nursery growing",
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Add two propagation cores (prudentium, wax and a living matrix each), budgeted apart from the imperium and capsules.",
    "The greenhouse recipe again, doubled. Juan's nursery is the one part of Heliodor that never stopped."
  ],
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.title": "The reserve's engine",
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Combine two sky ingots, two imperium essences, two ecosystem capsules and two propagation cores in a crafting grid. Eight slots make one renewal engine; Modern Industrialization's quantum circuits need one too.",
    "Juan's rule, built into a machine: take only what can grow back."
  ],
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.title": "Field note: take one, grow one",
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: take one bounded batch from your crops, your hive and your aura route, and let each recover before repeating. Confirm after trying it.",
    "Juan asks the question he has asked for years inside the light: will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.title": "Renewable Horizons",
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Deliver one renewal engine to Renewable Horizons in the Atlas.",
    "Juan, from inside the Entrelumen: 'Take only what can grow back before the next person needs it. I have fed a whole city on that rule.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.title": "Two meals before departure",
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Cook two Farmer's Delight fish stews in a cooking pot, from raw fish with tomato sauce and onion.",
    "Aurelia's charter for the Ark begins, surprisingly, with food. Whoever comes through must be fed."
  ],
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.title": "Something fresh on the shelf",
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Make two mixed salads from a leafy green, tomato, beetroot and bowl.",
    "A fresh plate on the charter's list, in Juan's hand. Aurelia signed underneath without changing a word."
  ],
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.title": "A count the next person can read",
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Add one AE2 calculation processor, printed in the Inscriber, to the Habitation Charter.",
    "Aurelia counts everything; it is how she governs. For once, the count is for the people arriving, not for the council."
  ],
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.title": "Food for the road and the return",
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Set aside two packs of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets each), apart from the stew and salad.",
    "The same rations Juan packed for the workshop's long shifts. This time they are for a door that opens both ways."
  ],
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.title": "A charter for an inhabited place",
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Combine two fish stews, two mixed salads, one calculation processor and two packs of Travel Rations: seven slots make one Habitation Charter, and the four bowls come back to you.",
    "Aurelia's seal on a promise: whoever crosses will find a place to live. She has not yet said what she wants in return."
  ],
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.title": "Field note: a room someone can use",
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: walk from your arrival point to a lit bed, a reachable kitchen and a pantry with readable stock, and ask whether a newcomer could manage alone. Confirm after the walk.",
    "Soon, people who have not walked in the sun for years will come through. Bodhi asks only that they feel welcome."
  ],
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.title": "A Place Worth Returning To",
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Deliver one Habitation Charter to A Place to Return To in the Atlas.",
    "The first day's sentence, complete at last. Terra: 'Make room for those who have not arrived yet. We are the ones.'"
  ],
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.title": "Field note: a visible pause",
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: if you enjoy ComputerCraft, build a small panel that shows a buffer's count and whether it is paused; a sign and a manual stop work just as well. Confirm after comparing it with the real container.",
    "Terra's workshop had a board like this on every wall. Nobody should have to guess whether a machine is running."
  ],
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.title": "A door, not a god",
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "When the three projects are recorded, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to World Network in the Atlas. The six module projects open next, in V · The Activation; there is no Advance here.",
    "The Ark's plan is complete: six modules around a controller that opens a rift in the light. Once you activate it, the Ark will forge the Light Key. Bodhi's only condition: 'Open it. Never own it.'"
  ],
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.title": "V · The Activation",
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six modules around a controller, six batches and one deliberate act: the Ark opens a seam in the light and forges the Light Key."
  ],
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.title": "The Ark takes shape",
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Build six different Ark modules, place them around the controller and commission them one batch at a time; activating the Ark forges the Light Key and opens act VI. This optional page only introduces the chapter: confirm when ready.",
    "Terra spreads the plan across the Atlas: six chambers, one for each discipline of Heliodor. 'The fusion wanted one machine to hold everything. This time, six hands hold one door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.title": "A controller, not a throne",
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Craft the Ark Controller shapelessly from one lodestone, one signal core and one diamond, and keep it: owning it records nothing. Place it where all six module blocks can stay nearby; a normal interaction reports the current batch and any missing block.",
    "Aurelia wanted a throne at the centre of the fusion machine. Terra built a controller instead: anyone can read it, and it obeys only a team that finished its work."
  ],
  "quest.6E755C961BFC8754.title": "A bus with a second path",
  "quest.6E755C961BFC8754.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Set aside two Mekanism atomic alloys for the Engineering Module. Its delivery also takes two calibration frames, two energy couplers and one Ark Connection Bus: the same seven parts as its crafting recipe, so a lost module can be made again.",
    "Terra draws a bypass beside every line of the Ark. The fusion machine had one path for everything, and nowhere to go when it failed."
  ],
  "quest.0AF7E5AD8DAA6FA2.title": "A boundary with a witness",
  "quest.0AF7E5AD8DAA6FA2.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Reserve two Occultism iesnium ingots. Iesnium hides as Nether netherrack: Otherworld Goggles reveal it and an Infused or Iesnium Pickaxe mines it; smelt the raw ore. Two spectral lenses and two containment seals complete the Arcane Module's delivery and recipe.",
    "Bodhi asks for a boundary around the strange light, with a window in it. 'Seal what could hurt us. Never seal it from sight.'"
  ],
  "quest.32C7CF38D764EF3C.title": "A reserve that answers",
  "quest.32C7CF38D764EF3C.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "The Nature Module takes one renewal engine, two ecosystem capsules and two living matrices; the same five inputs craft a replacement if the block is lost. Keep your settlement's own reserve where it is.",
    "Juan's rule, now inside the Ark: if one supply fails, a living system must be able to begin again. He learned it feeding a frozen city."
  ],
  "quest.2C387677AC04141E.title": "Routes with readable stores",
  "quest.2C387677AC04141E.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Prepare two routing matrices, two handling cores and one Ark Connection Bus for the Logistics Module. The same five inputs craft a replacement without reopening the one-time Atlas project; holding them only completes this lesson.",
    "Aurelia counts everything, and for once Terra agrees: before a route changes, anyone should be able to check what it carries."
  ],
  "quest.41D8D1F4B9303A79.title": "A room for whoever follows",
  "quest.41D8D1F4B9303A79.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Set aside one Habitation Charter, two packs of Travel Rations and two living matrices for the Habitation Module; the same five inputs craft a replacement later. Count these two packs apart from the eight the commissioning will ask for.",
    "Juan packed rations like these for Terra's long shifts. Aurelia signs for every pack: nobody crossing the light should arrive to an empty kitchen."
  ],
  "quest.2A320DF4401C30B7.title": "A chart with a return line",
  "quest.2A320DF4401C30B7.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "The Exploration Module takes one horizon chart, one spectral lens, two Twilight Forest steeleaf ingots and two Aether zanite gemstones. Search Hollow Hill chests for steeleaf (Labyrinth chests are a chance, not a promise) and mine zanite ore without Silk Touch.",
    "Terra draws the way home before the way in. The fusion's engineers never marked a return; the Ark's first line is one."
  ],
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.title": "The old doorway",
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Craft Eyes of Ender from ender pearls and blaze powder. A thrown eye leads toward a stronghold, and its portal frame needs eyes to open; bring enough for both. Carrying eyes only prepares the trip: your campaign still has to enter the End.",
    "The Atlas remembers this doorway from Heliodor's oldest charts. They never used it. They were too busy looking up."
  ],
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.title": "Field note: a way home",
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pack food, protection and blocks before the stronghold portal and agree on a return route. In a new End, defeating the dragon opens the exit home; on a shared world it may already be open, and your team needs no second kill. Confirm when you have a plan.",
    "Bodhi asks one thing of every journey: that it ends where it began, with everyone."
  ],
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.title": "A horizon actually crossed",
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Enter the End with your current team. The server witnesses real entry, login or respawn there; an earlier visit counts, even before act V. Joining a team does not bring your personal travels with you, and clicking this task does nothing.",
    "Terra needs the End's silence measured for the exploration module: the one place the light of the Aether never reached."
  ],
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.title": "Engineering: a path around failure",
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two calibration frames, two energy couplers, one Ark Connection Bus and two Mekanism atomic alloys to Engineering Module in the Atlas. Placed, an empty hand reads the team's diagnosis; a damaged tool with its repair material in the offhand gets a quarter of its durability back, no experience spent.",
    "Terra: 'Everything breaks. What matters is whether you can fix it.'"
  ],
  "quest.7B4CB4FC66705C6B.title": "Arcane: a boundary that holds",
  "quest.7B4CB4FC66705C6B.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two spectral lenses, two containment seals and two Occultism iesnium ingots to Arcane Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the team's field journal, takes its stabilization batch when crouch-used empty-handed, and splits a book of several enchantments into single volumes, one ordinary book per extra volume.",
    "Bodhi keeps the strange light behind glass: sealed, never hidden."
  ],
  "quest.32E5B9B04FF003DE.title": "Nature: growth with reserves",
  "quest.32E5B9B04FF003DE.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver one renewal engine, two ecosystem capsules and two living matrices to Nature Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the restoration journal and takes its batch when crouch-used empty-handed. Mark a site with a bookmarked compass; then bone meal and saplings bring back its biome's cover and trees, leaving built blocks alone.",
    "Juan: 'Take only what can grow back.'"
  ],
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.title": "Logistics: a count before movement",
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two routing matrices, two handling cores and one Ark Connection Bus to Logistics Module in the Atlas. Placed, an empty hand opens its 27-slot depot, crouching adds to the current Ark batch, and a routing matrix records and refills a personal expedition kit from the depot.",
    "Aurelia's ledger, turned outward: everyone can see what the Ark holds before they leave."
  ],
  "quest.0984C0DF0C9E836E.title": "Habitation: a place to arrive",
  "quest.0984C0DF0C9E836E.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver one Habitation Charter, two packs of Travel Rations and two living matrices to Habitation Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the supply journal and takes its provisioning batch when crouch-used empty-handed; used with a bed, it reserves a temporary respawn and keeps your old home.",
    "Aurelia promised a place to live to whoever crosses. Juan makes sure there is dinner."
  ],
  "quest.105A416A3980602B.title": "Exploration: the return marked first",
  "quest.105A416A3980602B.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network and a witnessed End arrival, deliver one horizon chart, one spectral lens, two Twilight Forest steeleaf ingots and two Aether zanite gemstones to Exploration Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the journey journal and takes the final chart when crouch-used; with a filled map, it fills blank pixels from your other maps of that area.",
    "Terra's charts all start with the way home."
  ],
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.title": "Field note: six blocks in reach",
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: place the controller and keep all six module blocks within three blocks horizontally, one below or two above it. Inspect the controller to see which ones it finds; the server checks the real blocks at every batch and at activation.",
    "Six chambers close enough to hear each other. Terra built the fusion machine as one piece; the Ark is six, side by side."
  ],
  "quest.790F7DA7C34DE333.title": "I · Calibrate the bypass",
  "quest.790F7DA7C34DE333.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "With all six module projects credited and their blocks around the controller, bring four additional calibration frames and two additional power regulators. Crouch and use the controller with an empty main hand; it takes what you carry toward the batch, and partial deposits survive a restart. Inspect it for the remainder.",
    "Terra checks every bypass twice. The fusion was never checked once."
  ],
  "quest.3FDD095D9F8F9109.title": "II · Hold the boundary",
  "quest.3FDD095D9F8F9109.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The second batch takes two additional containment seals at the controller, with the six module blocks still in place and the same crouched, empty-handed use. The first batch is already credited: repeating it takes nothing and skips nothing.",
    "Bodhi watches the seals settle. 'A boundary you can check again tomorrow is worth more than one you swear by today.'"
  ],
  "quest.0CC3F84AEB9FD36C.title": "III · Keep a living reserve",
  "quest.0CC3F84AEB9FD36C.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The third batch takes two additional ecosystem capsules. Deposit them with the six module blocks present; the server records each accepted amount and credits the step when the batch is complete.",
    "Juan will not call a reserve renewable because the diagram is green. He waits to see it grow back, the way he has waited inside the light for years."
  ],
  "quest.42B7C481E3710955.title": "IV · Route the first load",
  "quest.42B7C481E3710955.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The fourth batch takes two additional routing matrices, apart from the ones the Logistics Module consumed. A deposit can be partial; inspect the controller for the exact remainder before bringing more.",
    "Aurelia wants the Ark's routes legible even after someone leaves the team. It is the first rule of hers Terra ever agreed with."
  ],
  "quest.63EF631DCCEDFEC9.title": "V · Provision a welcome",
  "quest.63EF631DCCEDFEC9.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The fifth batch takes eight more packs of Travel Rations, apart from the two the Habitation Module used. Keep every module block in place and deposit them crouching with an empty main hand.",
    "Juan's arithmetic is blunt: a door that brings people through must also feed them when they arrive, without quietly emptying the kitchen at home."
  ],
  "quest.2924970994B829D6.title": "VI · Chart a return",
  "quest.2924970994B829D6.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The sixth and last batch takes one additional horizon chart, apart from the one the Exploration Module consumed. After it, inspect the controller: six batches can be complete while the activation still waits for your explicit choice.",
    "Terra folds the chart so the route home stays on its outer face. 'Whoever crosses should always see the way back.'"
  ],
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.title": "The Ark opens the light",
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "After six credited batches, with World Network complete, the End journey witnessed and all six modules beside the controller, crouch and interact with it once more with an empty main hand. That act activates the Ark, consumes nothing and forges your team's Light Key. Act VI begins.",
    "The light parts along a seam. Bodhi, very quietly: 'Open it. Never own it.' Behind it, Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.title": "Afterward: two routes",
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: make two different ways to move one useful supply between your settlements, then pause one and see whether the other is understandable and usable. Note what failed and what was easy to repair.",
    "Terra's favourite test, older than the fusion: a system is only as good as its second path."
  ],
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.title": "Afterward: a shared reserve",
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pick one renewable food or material reserve, let a visitor take a known amount and time how long your usual process takes to replace it. Note what would make the reserve fair to share.",
    "Juan's question, the one he asks Solsticio every morning: if someone new arrives today, will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.title": "VI · Solsticio",
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The capital of Heliodor, frozen inside the Entrelumen. Cross with the Light Key: the voices are waiting in person."
  ],
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.title": "Inside the light",
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.quest_desc": [
    "The Light Key · The crossing",
    "",
    "Hold use with your Light Key until the ring of light closes: it carries you into Solsticio once and breaks as you cross, leaving a return key bound to you. The server records your own team's arrival in the city; visits through another team's portal do not count.",
    "Noon that never ends, over copper and glass. Nobody here has aged a day. Terra is already waving, and the whole city turns to look at you."
  ],
  "chapter.551D4E474ABCF322.title": "An Inventory That Remembers",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.title": "Self-check: Two columns in the margin",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.quest_desc": [
    "Mara's margin",
    "",
    "After the first light answered, Mara drew TAKE and LEAVE beside the map. Choose one supply to carry through a hurried return and one material to leave at the workshop. Decide which column each belongs in, then mark this note.",
    "These notes are optional. A square fills when you carry its item and takes nothing from you; a circle is yours to mark after you try its exercise. Neither holds up the journey."
  ],
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.title": "A bag for the road",
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Make a basic Sophisticated Backpack with leather, string and a wooden chest; check the recipe for their placement. Put an ordinary block inside, close the bag, then find and remove it again. Look for the backpack action under Controls if you want quick access. This basic bag is enough for the exercises ahead."
  ],
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.title": "A place that stays",
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Combine an ordinary chest and a lever to make a Sophisticated Storage chest. Set it beside the bench you use and give it one job: incoming stone, repair supplies or food for the next journey. Put a matching stack inside and leave room for your return. The bag travels with you; this chest tells anyone coming home where to look."
  ],
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.title": "Self-check: What must stay aboard",
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Pack food for a short trip and a spare tool in places you can remember. Keep the working tool within reach; the spare is for a broken handle. Leave a food reserve at home so an empty return can still lead to another departure.",
    "Before you leave, open the bag and the home chest and point to each reserve. Mark this note when you can find both without searching every slot."
  ],
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.title": "Self-check: An empty slot with a name",
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "In the chest's settings, set Memory on one slot holding a common workshop material. Remove its last stack, then try putting the same material and a different one back. Notice where each goes. If the result differs from your plan, revisit the slot and its setting before using scarce stock. The empty space can keep a place for tomorrow's stone."
  ],
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.title": "The bag learns to gather",
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic Pickup Upgrade uses an Upgrade Base, a sticky piston, string and redstone; check the recipe viewer for their placement. Put it in the backpack's upgrade slot and open its settings. Start with one plentiful block in the filter. Leave rare tools out of the first ground test; the next note follows two ordinary drops."
  ],
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.title": "A second stack within reach",
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The Refill Upgrade can supply a selected inventory stack from the backpack. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, an ender pearl, a chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer before crafting it. Keep spare torches in the bag for the first trial: each torch you use leaves a gap you can see. Keep another reserve at home before relying on the bag in a cave."
  ],
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.title": "A rule at the workshop door",
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Make a Sophisticated Storage Filter Upgrade for the workshop chest. It governs items moved into or out of storage by a hopper or other transport; the backpack's Pickup Upgrade has a different job. Choose one plentiful block to allow and another cheap block to reject, then set the rule in the upgrade's controls. Test both before sending scarce materials through."
  ],
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.title": "A shared doorstep",
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "A Storage Controller gives connected Sophisticated Storage blocks one place for deposits and external item transfer. Its recipe starts with a wooden storage block and comparators; check the recipe viewer for the arrangement. Place it near two stores you can inspect easily, with a different common material in each. Keep the individual stores useful so you can trace a deposit to its shelf."
  ],
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.title": "Self-check: Two drops, one decision",
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Install Pickup and set its filter for one plentiful block. In a safe place, drop that block and a different expendable item, one at a time. Look in the backpack, your inventory and the ground to find both. If the route surprises you, adjust the filter and repeat with cheap materials. Mark this note when you can account for both drops."
  ],
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.title": "Self-check: The last torch is visible",
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic backpack has one upgrade slot. Remove Pickup or the previous upgrade and install Refill. Put spare torches in the bag and select torches in Refill's settings. Use one from your inventory, then compare the carried stack with the bag's reserve. Remove the spare torches and repeat to see what happens when the reserve runs out. Keep food and the spare tool in their own places, ready for the trip home."
  ],
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.title": "Self-check: The chest accepts one kind",
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Fit the Filter Upgrade to the workshop chest and feed it through a hopper. Try one permitted block, then one rejected block, separately. Check the hopper and chest after each attempt; a rejected item may wait upstream. Manual insertion and piped insertion can follow different rules. Mark this note once you know where both blocks ended, and clear the hopper before a real batch."
  ],
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.title": "Self-check: One entrance, two shelves",
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Place the controller beside two connected Sophisticated Storage blocks. Put a different ordinary material in each store, then make a small deposit through the controller. Find the deposited items in the physical stores and take them back out. If nothing moves, inspect the connections before adding more shelves. Mark this note after you can follow the route in both directions."
  ],
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.title": "The return has a gesture",
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "The Backpack Deposit Upgrade moves items from the bag into an inventory you sneak-right-click. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, a piston, a wooden chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer for the layout. Put ordinary stone in the workshop chest and in your bag before trying Match Inventory Contents. Keep food and a spare tool in the bag so you can see what stays with you."
  ],
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.title": "Self-check: The bag comes home lighter",
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "Swap the previous upgrade for Deposit in the basic backpack's single upgrade slot. Put a small stack of stone in the bag beside the food and spare tool you chose to keep. Stock the workshop chest with stone, set Deposit to Match Inventory Contents, and sneak-right-click that chest with the bag. Count stone in both places, then check the food and tool. If the result surprises you, retrieve the items and repeat with cheap stock. Mark this note after the travel reserve stays aboard."
  ],
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.title": "Self-check: A shelf after the network",
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.quest_desc": [
    "One shelf stays local",
    "",
    "Sera's later sketches show a digital network; Mara keeps a physical shelf beside the bench. When you have AE2, close its terminal and take one food stack and one repair supply from that local shelf. Decide which reserve should remain within reach if the network is unavailable. Mark this note after you can retrieve both without the terminal, then restock the shelf for the next return."
  ]
}
